Input: {"question": "Which person or organization did Lyron J Winderbaum work for?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 189, "text": "As I walked through the bustling streets of Leeds, the grandeur of the University of Leeds' Parkinson Building loomed before me, its imposing clock tower a beacon of intellectual curiosity."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 190, "end": 219, "text": "I had an appointment with Dr."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 220, "end": 361, "text": "Lyron J Winderbaum, a renowned researcher in the field of environmental science, and I was eager to learn more about his groundbreaking work."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 362, "end": 427, "text": "As I entered the building, I was greeted by the warm smile of Dr."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 428, "end": 484, "text": "Winderbaum himself, who was waiting for me in the foyer."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 485, "end": 613, "text": "His eyes twinkled behind a pair of wire-rimmed glasses, and his wild shock of curly brown hair seemed to have a life of its own."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 614, "end": 743, "text": "We exchanged pleasantries, and he led me to his office, nestled in the heart of the university's School of Earth and Environment."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 744, "end": 845, "text": "The room was a treasure trove of eclectic trinkets and mementos, each one telling a story of its own."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 846, "end": 1014, "text": "A faded poster of the Amazon rainforest adorned one wall, while a shelf overflowing with dog-eared textbooks and journals seemed to groan under the weight of knowledge."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1015, "end": 1121, "text": "In the corner, a small, potted fern struggled to thrive under the fluorescent lighting, a testament to Dr."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1122, "end": 1165, "text": "Winderbaum's passion for the natural world."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1166, "end": 1185, "text": "As we sat down, Dr."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1186, "end": 1284, "text": "Winderbaum leaned back in his chair, steepling his fingers together in a gesture of contemplation."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1285, "end": 1354, "text": "\"So, you're interested in my work on sustainable land use practices?\""}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1355, "end": 1393, "text": "he asked, his voice warm and engaging."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1394, "end": 1523, "text": "I nodded, and he launched into a passionate discourse on the importance of preserving biodiversity in the face of climate change."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1524, "end": 1719, "text": "As he spoke, I couldn't help but notice the small, silver pin on his lapel – the emblem of the University of Leeds, a subtle yet telling detail that spoke to his affiliation with the institution."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1720, "end": 1820, "text": "It was a small thing, perhaps, but it seemed to underscore the sense of pride and belonging that Dr."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1821, "end": 1863, "text": "Winderbaum felt towards his academic home."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1864, "end": 1904, "text": "As our conversation drew to a close, Dr."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1905, "end": 2012, "text": "Winderbaum walked me out of the building, pointing out the various landmarks and hidden gems of the campus."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "st